{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q416285","formula":"C₆H₆O₄","hill":"C6H6O4","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":6.0,"H":6.0,"O":4.0},"names":{"en":"Kojic acid","ru":"Койевая кислота"},"descriptions":{"en":"Kojic acid is an organic compound with the formula HOCH2C5H2O2OH. It is a derivative of 4-pyrone that functions in nature as a chelation agent produced by several species of fungus, especially Aspergillus oryzae, which has the Japanese common name koji. Kojic acid is a by-product in the fermentation process of malting rice, for use in the manufacturing of sake, the Japanese rice wine. It is a mild inhibitor of the formation of pigment in plant and animal tissues, and is used in food and cosmetics to preserve or change colors of substances.","ru":"Койевая кислота (от яп. 麹 /kōji/ — койи) — органическое соединение, представляет собой гидроксильное производное γ-пирона (кетопроизводное пирана)."},"fame":25,"pubchemCid":3840,"mass":142.11,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=C(OC=C(C1=O)O)CO","inchikey":"BEJNERDRQOWKJM-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"5-hydroxy-2-(hydroxymethyl)pyran-4-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"3840","atoms":16,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.838,"y":1.096,"z":0.201,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.282,"y":0.333,"z":-0.563,"el":"O"},{"x":2.81,"y":1.04,"z":-0.117,"el":"O"},{"x":2.087,"y":-1.684,"z":-0.14,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.147,"y":-0.256,"z":0.187,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.22,"y":-1.218,"z":0.077,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.608,"y":-0.547,"z":0.309,"el":"C"},{"x":1.207,"y":-0.838,"z":-0.035,"el":"C"},{"x":1.508,"y":0.612,"z":-0.017,"el":"C"},{"x":0.482,"y":1.462,"z":0.099,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.47,"y":-2.272,"z":0.069,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.946,"y":-0.36,"z":1.333,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.85,"y":-1.578,"z":0.033,"el":"H"},{"x":0.582,"y":2.539,"z":0.123,"el":"H"},{"x":-4.234,"y":0.157,"z":-